Perfect. As a QA Automation Engineer, don't just know the file names. Know:

**1. Why the file exists**
**2. Who calls it**
**3. What it contains**
**4. When it gets triggered**

---

# 1. BaseClass.java

### Purpose : Common setup and teardown for all tests.

### Contains

```java
@BeforeMethod
public void setup()

@AfterMethod
public void tearDown()
```

### Why Needed : Without BaseClass, every test would need:

```java
ChromeDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
driver.get(url);
driver.quit();
```

again and again.

### Triggered By

```text
LoginTest extends BaseClass
```

When TestNG starts the test:

```text
LoginTest
   ↓
@BeforeMethod (BaseClass)
   ↓
Test Method
   ↓
@AfterMethod (BaseClass)
```

---
====================================================================================
# 2. DriverFactory.java

### Purpose: Create browser instance.

### Contains

```java
ChromeDriver

EdgeDriver

FirefoxDriver
```

Example:

```java
public static WebDriver getDriver()
```

### Why Needed

Tomorrow manager says:
```text
Run on Edge Browser
```

Change only DriverFactory.

No need to modify all test cases.

### Triggered By

```text
BaseClass
   ↓
DriverFactory
```

---
===================================================================================================
# 3. LoginPage.java

### Purpose : Store Login Page Locators + Actions.

### Contains

```java
@FindBy(id="username")
WebElement username;

@FindBy(id="password")
WebElement password;
```

Methods:

```java
enterUsername()

enterPassword()

clickLogin()
```

### Why Needed

Avoid:

```java
driver.findElement()
```

inside test cases.

### Triggered By

```text
LoginTest
   ↓
LoginPage
```

---
================================================================================================
# 4. DashboardPage.java

### Purpose: Store Dashboard related actions.

### Contains

```java
verifyDashboard()

logout()

clickProfile()
```

### Why Needed

After login user lands on dashboard.

Dashboard operations belong here.

### Triggered By

```text
LoginPage
    ↓
DashboardPage
```

---
================================================================================================
# 5. CommonMethods.java

### Purpose: Reusable methods.

### Contains

```java
click()

sendKeys()

scroll()

uploadFile()

selectDropdown()
```

### Why Needed

Without it:

```java
element.click();
element.click();
element.click();
```

in every page.

### Triggered By

```text
LoginPage
DashboardPage

      ↓

CommonMethods
```

---
======================================================================================
# 6. ConfigReader.java

### Purpose: Read config.properties.

### Contains

```java
getProperty()
```

### Reads

```properties
browser=chrome
url=https://abc.com
```

### Why Needed

Avoid hardcoding.

Bad:

```java
driver.get("https://abc.com");
```

Good:

```java
driver.get(getProperty("url"));
```

### Triggered By

```text
BaseClass
      ↓
ConfigReader
```

---

# 7. ExcelUtils.java

### Purpose

Read Excel.

### Contains

```java
getRowCount()

getCellData()
```

### Why Needed

Store test data outside code.

Example:

```text
Admin admin123

User1 pass123
```

### Triggered By

```text
TestDataProvider
      ↓
ExcelUtils
```

---
================================================================================================
# 8. WaitUtils.java

### Purpose: Handle synchronization.

### Contains

```java
waitForElementVisible()

waitForElementClickable()
```

### Why Needed

Web pages load slowly.

Without wait:

```java
NoSuchElementException
```

### Triggered By

```text
LoginPage
DashboardPage
```

---
==================================================================================
# 9. ScreenshotUtils.java

### Purpose: Take screenshot.

### Contains

```java
captureScreenshot()
```

### Why Needed

Evidence when test fails.

Saved In:

```text
reports/Screenshots
```

### Triggered By

```text
TestListener
      ↓
ScreenshotUtils
```

---
===============================================================================================
# 10. TestListener.java

### Purpose: Listen to test execution.

### Contains

```java
onTestStart()

onTestSuccess()

onTestFailure()
```

### Why Needed

Automatic actions.

Example:

```text
Test Failed
      ↓
Take Screenshot
      ↓
Update Report
```

### Triggered By

```text
TestNG
      ↓
Listener
```

You never call it manually.

---
===================================================================================================
# 11. TestDataProvider.java

### Purpose

Provide test data.

### Contains

```java
@DataProvider
```

Example:

```java
{
 {"admin","admin123"},
 {"user","user123"}
}
```

### Why Needed

Run same test multiple times.

### Triggered By

```java
@Test(dataProvider="loginData")
```

---=========================================================================================================
# 12. LoginTest.java

### Purpose: Actual Test Case.

### Contains

```java
@Test
public void verifyLogin()
```

### Why Needed

This is where testing happens.

### Triggered By

```text
TestNG XML
      ↓
LoginTest
```

---
=============================================================================================
# 13. config.properties

### Purpose: Store environment configuration.

### Contains

```properties
browser=chrome
url=https://test.com
username=admin
password=admin123
```

### Read By

```text
ConfigReader
```

---

# Actual Execution Flow

```text
testng.xml

      ↓

LoginTest

      ↓

BaseClass

      ↓

DriverFactory

      ↓

Chrome Browser Opens

      ↓

ConfigReader

      ↓

Read URL

      ↓

LoginPage

      ↓

CommonMethods

      ↓

Enter Username

      ↓

Enter Password

      ↓

Click Login

      ↓

DashboardPage

      ↓

Assertion

      ↓

PASS / FAIL

      ↓

TestListener

      ↓

Extent Report

      ↓

ScreenshotUtils (only if fail)

      ↓

reports folder
```

### Interview One-Liner

If asked, *"How do all files connect?"*

> Test execution starts from TestNG test cases. Test cases extend BaseClass, which initializes the browser using DriverFactory and reads configuration through ConfigReader. Test cases interact with Page Objects such as LoginPage and DashboardPage. CommonMethods and WaitUtils provide reusable actions. Test data is supplied through DataProvider and ExcelUtils. TestNG Listeners monitor execution and generate reports or screenshots using ScreenshotUtils when failures occur. This design follows the Page Object Model and keeps the framework maintainable and reusable.
